G3705.b:
⟪ὅραμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< ὁράω), [in LXX for ⁨חָזוֹן⁩, ⁨מַרְאֶה⁩, etc.;] ⟪that which is seen⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a sight⟫, ⟪spectacle⟫: ⟦Matthew 17:9|Mt 17:9⟧, ⟦Acts 7:31|Ac 7:31⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪an appearance⟫, ⟪vision⟫: ⟦Acts 9:10|Ac 9:10⟧, ⟦Acts 9:12|12⟧(Rec.) ⟦Acts 10:3|10:3⟧, ⟦Acts 10:17|17⟧, ⟦Acts 10:19|19⟧ ⟦Acts 11:5|11:5⟧ ⟦Acts 12:9|12:9⟧ ⟦Acts 16:9|16:9⟧, ⟦Acts 16:10|10⟧ ⟦Acts 18:9|18:9⟧ (cf. ὀπτασία).†

G3709.b:
⟪ὀργή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אַף⁩, also for ⁨חָרוֹן⁩, ⁨חֵמָה⁩, ⁨קֶצֶף⁩, etc.;]
⟪1⟫ ⟪impulse⟫, ⟪propensity⟫, ⟪disposition⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪anger⟫, ⟪wrath⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of men: ⟦Mark 3:5|Mk 3:5⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:31|Eph 4:31⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:8|Col 3:8⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 2:8|I Ti 2:8⟧, ⟦James 1:19|Ja 1:19⟧, ⟦James 1:20|20⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of God;
		⟪α⟫ that reaction of the divine nature against sin which in anthropomorphic language is called ⟪anger⟫: ⟦Romans 1:18|Ro 1:18⟧ ⟦Romans 9:22|9:22⟧ ⟦Romans 12:19|12:19⟧, (ICC, in l.), ⟦1 Thessalonians 1:10|I Th 1:10⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:16|2:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:11|He 3:11⟧ ⟦Hebrews 4:3|4:3⟧(LXX), ⟦Revelation 14:10|Re 14:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:19|16:19⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:15|19:15⟧;
		⟪β⟫ of the effect of God's anger: ⟦Matthew 3:7|Mt 3:7⟧, ⟦Luke 3:7|Lk 3:7⟧ ⟦Luke 21:23|21:23⟧, ⟦John 3:36|Jo 3:36⟧, ⟦Romans 2:5|Ro 2:5⟧, ⟦Romans 2:8|8⟧ ⟦Romans 3:5|3:5⟧ ⟦Romans 4:15|4:15⟧ ⟦Romans 5:9|5:9⟧ ⟦Romans 13:4|13:4⟧, ⟦Romans 13:5|5⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:6|Eph 5:6⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:6|Col 3:6⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:9|I Th 5:9⟧, ⟦James 1:20|Ja 1:20⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:16|Re 6:16⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:17|17⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:18|11:18⟧; σκεύη ὀργῆς, ⟦Romans 9:22|Ro 9:22⟧; τέκνα ὀργῆς, ⟦Ephesians 2:3|Eph 2:3⟧.†
SYN.: v.s. θυμός.

G3717.b:
⟪ὀρθός⟫, -ή, -όν,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨יָשָׁר⁩;] ⟪straight⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in height, ⟪straight⟫, ⟪upright⟫: ⟦Acts 14:10|Ac 14:10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in line, ⟪straight⟫, ⟪direct⟫: fig., ⟦Hebrews 12:13|He 12:13⟧(LXX).†

G3745.b:
⟪ὅσος⟫, -η, -ον,
correlat. of τοσοῦτος, ⟪how much⟫, ⟪how many⟫, ⟪how great⟫, ⟪how far⟫, ⟪how long⟫, ⟪as much as⟫, etc. (= Lat. quantus);
⟪(a)⟫ of number and quantity: m. pl., ⟦Matthew 14:36|Mt 14:36⟧, ⟦Mark 3:10|Mk 3:10⟧, ⟦Romans 2:12|Ro 2:12⟧, al.; n. pl., ⟦Matthew 17:12|Mt 17:12⟧, ⟦Mark 10:21|Mk 10:21⟧, ⟦Luke 11:8|Lk 11:8⟧, al.; πάτνες (πάντα) ὅ., ⟦Matthew 13:46|Mt 13:46⟧, ⟦Luke 4:40|Lk 4:40⟧, al.; seq. οὗτοι (ταῦτα), ⟦Romans 8:14|Ro 8:14⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:8|Phl 4:8⟧; c. indic., ⟦Mark 6:56|Mk 6:56⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:19|Re 3:19⟧; c. subjc. ⟦Mark 3:28|Mk 3:28⟧, al.; ὅ. ἄν, ⟦Matthew 18:18|Mt 18:18⟧, ⟦John 11:22|Jo 11:22⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ of measure and degree: ⟦Mark 3:8|Mk 3:8⟧, ⟦Luke 8:39|Lk 8:39⟧, ⟦Acts 9:13|Ac 9:13⟧; in compar. sent., ὅσον seq. μᾶλλον, ⟦Mark 7:36|Mk 7:36⟧; καθ’ ὅσον, c. compar., ⟦Hebrews 3:3|He 3:3⟧; seq. τοσοῦτο, ⟦Hebrews 7:20|He 7:20⟧; οὕτως, ⟦Hebrews 9:27|He 9:27⟧; τοσούτῳ, c. compar. seq. ὅσῳ, c. compar., ⟦Hebrews 1:4|He 1:4⟧; ἐφ’ ὅσον, ⟪inasmuch as⟫, ⟦Matthew 25:40|Mt 25:40⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:45|45⟧, ⟦Romans 11:13|Ro 11:13⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of space and time: ⟦Revelation 21:16|Re 21:16⟧; ἐφ’ ὅσον, ⟪as long as⟫, ⟦Matthew 9:15|Mt 9:15⟧, ⟦2 Peter 1:13|II Pe 1:13⟧; ἐφ’ ὅ. χρόνον, ⟦Romans 7:1|Ro 7:1⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:39|I Co 7:39⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:1|Ga 4:1⟧; ἔτι μικρὸν ὅσον ὅσον, ⟪yet how very short a time⟫, ⟦Hebrews 10:37|He 10:37⟧(LXX).

G3748.b:
⟪ὅστις⟫, ἥτις, ὅ τι (also written ὅ, τι and ὅτι; v. LS, s.v.; WH, § 411; Tdf., Pr., 111), in NT scarcely ever except in nom. (M, Pr., 91), the only instance of the oblique cases being found in ἕως ὅτου (v.s. ἕως), relative of indef. reference (related to simple ὅς as Lat. quisquis to qui), ⟪whoever⟫, ⟪anyone who⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of an indef. person or thing: in general statements, ⟦Matthew 5:39|Mt 5:39⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:41|41⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:12|13:12⟧, and freq., ⟦Luke 14:27|Lk 14:27⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:4|Ga 5:4⟧, al.; in relative sentences, ⟦Matthew 7:26|Mt 7:26⟧, ⟦Luke 15:7|Lk 15:7⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:7|Phl 3:7⟧, al.; πᾶς ὅ., c. indic., ⟦Matthew 7:24|Mt 7:24⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:32|10:32⟧; ὅ ἄν (ἐάν), c. subjc., ⟦Matthew 12:50|Mt 12:50⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:12|13:12⟧, ⟦John 14:13|Jo 14:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:2|I Co 16:2⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:10|Ga 5:10⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ of a definite person or thing, indicating quality, "either generic, which, as other like things, or essential, which by its very nature" (Hort on ⟦1 Peter 2:11|I Pe 2:11⟧), ⟪who is such as⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:6|Mt 2:6⟧ ⟦Matthew 7:26|7:26⟧, ⟦Luke 2:10|Lk 2:10⟧ ⟦Luke 7:37|7:37⟧, ⟦John 8:53|Jo 8:53⟧, ⟦Acts 7:53|Ac 7:53⟧, ⟦Romans 6:2|Ro 6:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:17|I Co 3:17⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:24|Ga 4:24⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:23|Eph 1:23⟧, al.;
⟪(c)⟫ where the relative sentence expresses a reason, consequence, etc. (M, Pr., 92), ⟪seeing that he⟫ (⟪it⟫, ⟪they⟫), ⟪and he⟫ (⟪it⟫, ⟪they⟫): ⟦Luke 8:3|Lk 8:3⟧ ⟦Luke 10:42|10:42⟧, ⟦Acts 10:47|Ac 10:47⟧ ⟦Acts 11:28|11:28⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:3|Phl 4:3⟧, al.;
⟪(d)⟫ as in Ionic and late Greek (Bl., § 50, 1; M, Pr., 91), differing but little from ὅς: ⟦Luke 2:4|Lk 2:4⟧ ⟦Luke 9:30|9:30⟧, ⟦Acts 17:10|Ac 17:10⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:13|Re 12:13⟧.

G3752.b:
⟪ὅταν⟫ (for ὅτ’ ἄν = ὅτε ἄν), temporal particle, with a conditional sense, usually of things expected to occur in an indefinite future;
⟪1.⟫ prop., ⟪whenever⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ c. subjc. praes.: ⟦Matthew 6:2|Mt 6:2⟧, ⟦Matthew 6:5|5⟧, ⟦Mark 14:7|Mk 14:7⟧, ⟦Luke 11:36|Lk 11:36⟧, ⟦John 7:27|Jo 7:27⟧, ⟦Acts 23:35|Ac 23:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:4|I Co 3:4⟧, al.; ἕως τ. ἡμέρας ἐκείνης, ὅ., ⟦Matthew 26:29|Mt 26:29⟧, ⟦Mark 14:25|Mk 14:25⟧; seq. τότε, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:3|I Th 5:3⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ c. subjc. aor. (M, Pr., 185): ⟦Matthew 5:11|Mt 5:11⟧, ⟦Mark 4:15|Mk 4:15⟧, ⟦Luke 6:22|Lk 6:22⟧, ⟦John 2:10|Jo 2:10⟧ ⟦John 8:28|8:28⟧ (Field, Notes, 94), ⟦John 10:4|10:4⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ As in Hom. (LS, s.v.), but not in cl. prose, c. indic., ⟪when⟫ (M, Pr., 167 f.; Bl., § 65, 9): c. impf., ⟦Mark 3:11|Mk 3:11⟧(cf. ⟦Genesis 38:9|Ge 38:9⟧, al.); c. praes., ⟦Mark 11:25|Mk 11:25⟧; c. fut., ⟦Revelation 4:9|Re 4:9⟧ (Swete, in l.); c. aor., ⟦Mark 11:19|Mk 11:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:1|Re 8:1⟧ (Swete, in ll.; M, Pr., 168, 248; Field, Notes, 35).

G3754.b:
⟪ὅτι⟫, conjc. (prop. neut. of ὅστις).
⟪I.⟫ As conjc, introducing an objective clause, ⟪that⟫;
	⟪1.⟫ after verbs of seeing, knowing, thinking, saying, feeling: ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:32|6:32⟧ ⟦Matthew 11:25|11:25⟧, ⟦Mark 3:28|Mk 3:28⟧, ⟦Luke 2:49|Lk 2:49⟧, ⟦John 2:22|Jo 2:22⟧, ⟦Acts 4:13|Ac 4:13⟧, ⟦Romans 1:13|Ro 1:13⟧ ⟦Romans 8:38|8:38⟧ ⟦Romans 10:9|10:9⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:15|Phl 4:15⟧, ⟦James 2:24|Ja 2:24⟧, al.; elliptically, ⟦John 6:46|Jo 6:46⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:12|Phl 3:12⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ After εἶναι (γίνεσθαι): defining a demonstr. or pers. pron., ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧ ⟦John 16:19|16:19⟧, ⟦Romans 9:6|Ro 9:6⟧, ⟦1 John 3:16|I Jo 3:16⟧ al.; c. pron. interrog., ⟦Matthew 8:27|Mt 8:27⟧, ⟦Mark 4:41|Mk 4:41⟧, ⟦Luke 4:36|Lk 4:36⟧, ⟦John 4:22|Jo 4:22⟧ al.; id. elliptically, ⟦Luke 2:49|Lk 2:49⟧, ⟦Acts 5:4|Ac 5:4⟧, ⟦Acts 5:9|9⟧, al.;
	⟪3.⟫ Untranslatable, before direct discourse (ὅτι recitantis): ⟦Matthew 7:23|Mt 7:23⟧, ⟦Mark 2:16|Mk 2:16⟧, ⟦Luke 1:61|Lk 1:61⟧, ⟦John 1:20|Jo 1:20⟧, ⟦Acts 15:1|Ac 15:1⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:18|He 11:18⟧, al. (on the pleonastic ὡς ὅτι, v.s. ὡς).
⟪II.⟫ As causal particle, ⟪for that⟫, ⟪because⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:4|Mt 5:4-12⟧, ⟦Luke 6:20|Lk 6:20⟧, ⟦Luke 6:21|21⟧, ⟦John 1:30|Jo 1:30⟧ ⟦John 5:27|5:27⟧, ⟦Acts 1:5|Ac 1:5⟧, ⟦1 John 4:18|I Jo 4:18⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:10|Re 3:10⟧, al. mult.; διὰ τοῦτο ὅτι, ⟦John 8:47|Jo 8:47⟧ ⟦John 10:17|10:17⟧, al.; answering a question (διὰ τί), ⟦Romans 9:32|Ro 9:32⟧, al.; οὐκ ὅτι . . . ἀλλ’ ὅτι, ⟦John 6:26|Jo 6:26⟧ ⟦John 12:6|12:6⟧.

G3757.b:
⟪οὗ⟫
(prop. gen. of ὅς), adv. of place, ⟪where⟫, ⟪whither⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in answer to the question "where?" (= ubi): ⟦Matthew 2:9|Mt 2:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 18:20|18:20⟧, ⟦Luke 4:16|Lk 4:16⟧, ⟦Luke 4:17|17⟧ ⟦Luke 23:53|23:53⟧, ⟦Acts 1:13|Ac 1:13⟧ ⟦Acts 2:2|2:2⟧ ⟦Acts 7:29|7:29⟧ ⟦Acts 12:12|12:12⟧ ⟦Acts 16:13|16:13⟧ ⟦Acts 20:6|20:6⟧, ⟦Acts 20:8|8⟧ ⟦Acts 25:10|25:10⟧ ⟦Acts 28:14|28:14⟧, ⟦Romans 9:26|Ro 9:26⟧(LXX), ⟦Colossians 3:1|Col 3:1⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:9|He 3:9⟧(LXX), ⟦Revelation 17:15|Re 17:15⟧; of condition, ⟦Romans 4:15|Ro 4:15⟧ ⟦Romans 5:20|5:20⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:17|II Co 3:17⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in answer to the question "whither?" (= quo): ⟦Matthew 28:16|Mt 28:16⟧, ⟦Luke 10:1|Lk 10:1⟧ ⟦Luke 24:28|24:28⟧; seq. ἐάν, c. subjc., ⟦1 Corinthians 16:6|I Co 16:6⟧.†

G3778.b:
⟪οὗτος⟫, αὕτη, τοῦτο, gen., τούτου, ταύτης, τούτου,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨זֶה⁩, ⁨זֹאת⁩;] demonstr. pron. (related to ἐκεῖνος as hic to ille), ⟪this⟫;
⟪1.⟫ as subst., ⟪this one⟫, ⟪he⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ absol.: ⟦Matthew 3:17|Mt 3:17⟧, ⟦Mark 9:7|Mk 9:7⟧, ⟦Luke 7:44|Lk 7:44⟧, ⟦Luke 7:45|45⟧, ⟦John 1:15|Jo 1:15⟧, ⟦Acts 2:15|Ac 2:15⟧, al.; expressing contempt (cl.), ⟦Matthew 13:55|Mt 13:55⟧, ⟦Matthew 13:56|56⟧, ⟦Mark 6:2|Mk 6:2⟧, ⟦Mark 6:3|3⟧, ⟦John 6:42|Jo 6:42⟧, al.; εἰς τοῦτο, ⟦Mark 1:38|Mk 1:38⟧, ⟦Romans 14:9|Ro 14:9⟧; μετὰ τοῦτο (ταῦτα; V. Westc. on ⟦John 5:1|Jo 5:1⟧), ⟦John 2:12|Jo 2:12⟧ ⟦John 11:7|11:7⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ epanaleptic (referring to what precedes): ⟦Matthew 5:19|Mt 5:19⟧, ⟦Mark 3:35|Mk 3:35⟧, ⟦Luke 9:48|Lk 9:48⟧, ⟦John 6:46|Jo 6:46⟧, ⟦Romans 7:10|Ro 7:10⟧, al.;
	⟪(c)⟫ proleptic (referring to what follows): seq. ἵνα (Bl., § 69, 6), ⟦Luke 1:43|Lk 1:43⟧, ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧ (and freq.) ⟦John 15:8|15:8⟧, ⟦Romans 14:9|Ro 14:9⟧, al.; seq. ὅτι, ⟦Luke 10:11|Lk 10:11⟧, ⟦John 9:30|Jo 9:30⟧, ⟦Acts 24:14|Ac 24:14⟧, ⟦Romans 2:3|Ro 2:3⟧, al.; ὅπως, ⟦Romans 9:17|Ro 9:17⟧; ἐάν, ⟦John 13:35|Jo 13:35⟧;
	⟪(d)⟫ special idioms: τοῦτο μὲν . . . τ. δέ (cl), ⟪partly . . . partly⟫, ⟦Hebrews 10:33|He 10:33⟧; καὶ τοῦτο (τοῦτον, ταῦτα), ⟪and that⟫ (⟪him⟫) ⟪too⟫, ⟦Romans 13:11|Ro 13:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:2|I Co 2:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:12|He 11:12⟧; τοῦτ’ ἐστιν, ⟪that is to say⟫, ⟦Matthew 27:46|Mt 27:46⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As adj., c. subst.;
	⟪(a)⟫ c. art.
		⟪(α)⟫ before the art.: ⟦Matthew 12:32|Mt 12:32⟧, ⟦Mark 9:29|Mk 9:29⟧, ⟦Luke 7:44|Lk 7:44⟧, ⟦John 4:15|Jo 4:15⟧, ⟦Romans 11:24|Ro 11:24⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:9|Re 19:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(β)⟫ after the noun: ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧, ⟦Mark 12:16|Mk 12:16⟧, ⟦Luke 11:31|Lk 11:31⟧, ⟦John 4:13|Jo 4:13⟧, ⟦Acts 6:13|Ac 6:13⟧, ⟦Romans 15:28|Ro 15:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:20|I Co 1:20⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:24|Re 2:24⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ c. subst. anarth. (with predicative force; Bl., § 49, 4): ⟦Luke 1:36|Lk 1:36⟧ ⟦Luke 2:2|2:2⟧ ⟦Luke 24:21|24:21⟧, ⟦John 2:11|Jo 2:11⟧ ⟦John 4:54|4:54⟧ ⟦John 21:14|21:14⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 13:1|II Co 13:1⟧.

G3780.b:
⟪οὐχί⟫,
strengthened form of οὐ, ⟪not⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in neg. sentences, ⟪not⟫, ⟪not at all⟫: ⟦Luke 1:60|Lk 1:60⟧ ⟦Luke 12:51|12:51⟧, ⟦John 13:10|Jo 13:10⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ more freq. in questions where an affirm. ans. is expected (Lat. nonne): ⟦Matthew 5:46|Mt 5:46⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:47|47⟧, ⟦Luke 6:39|Lk 6:39⟧, ⟦John 11:9|Jo 11:9⟧, al.

G3788.b:
⟪ὀφθαλμός⟫, -οῦ, ὁ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עַיִן⁩;] ⟪the eye⟫ (as in cl., chiefly pl.): ⟦Matthew 5:38|Mt 5:38⟧, ⟦Mark 9:47|Mk 9:47⟧, ⟦Luke 6:41|Lk 6:41⟧, ⟦John 9:6|Jo 9:6⟧, al.; τοὺς ὀ. ἐξορύθσσειν (fig.), ⟦Galatians 4:15|Ga 4:15⟧; ἐπᾶραι, ⟦Luke 6:20|Lk 6:20⟧, ⟦John 6:5|Jo 6:5⟧; ἀνοῖξα, ⟦Acts 9:40|Ac 9:40⟧; id., of restoring sight, ⟦Matthew 20:33|Mt 20:33⟧, ⟦John 9:10|Jo 9:10⟧, al.; ἐν ῥιπῇ ὀφθαλμοῦ, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:52|I Co 15:52⟧; by anthropom., of God, ⟦Hebrews 4:13|He 4:13⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:12|I Pe 3:12⟧; pleonastically (cf. Thackeray, Gr., 42 f.), εἶδον οἱ ὀ. μου, ⟦Luke 2:30|Lk 2:30⟧ (similarly, ⟦Luke 4:20|Lk 4:20⟧ ⟦Luke 10:23|10:23⟧, ⟦John 12:40|Jo 12:40⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:9|I Co 2:9⟧, ⟦1 John 1:1|I Jo 1:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:7|Re 1:7⟧). Metaph. (as otherwise in cl.; v. LS, s.v.);
⟪(a)⟫ of ethical qualities: ὀ. πονηρός (meton., for envy; cf. Heb. ⁨עַיִן רַע⁩, ⟦Proverbs 28:22|Pr 28:22⟧; cf. Si 14:10 34:13), ⟦Matthew 6:22|Mt 6:22⟧, ⟦Matthew 6:23|23⟧, ⟦Mark 7:22|Mk 7:22⟧, ⟦Luke 11:34|Lk 11:34⟧; ἁπλοῦς, ⟦Matthew 6:22|Mt 6:22⟧, ⟦Luke 11:34|Lk 11:34⟧; ἐπιθυμία (q.v.) ὀφθαλμῶν (cf. ⟦Ecclesiastes 4:8|Ec 4:8⟧, Si 14:9), ⟦1 John 2:16|I Jo 2:16⟧; ὀ. μεστοὶ μοιχαλἰδος, ⟦2 Peter 2:14|II Pe 2:14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of mental vision: ⟦Matthew 13:15|Mt 13:15⟧, ⟦Mark 8:18|Mk 8:18⟧, ⟦Luke 19:42|Lk 19:42⟧, ⟦John 12:40|Jo 12:40⟧, ⟦Romans 11:8|Ro 11:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:1|Ga 3:1⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:18|Eph 1:18⟧, al.; ἐν ὀφθαλμοῖς seq. gen. (on the absence of the art., v.Bl., § 46, 9n; M, Pr., 81), ⟦Matthew 21:42|Mt 21:42⟧, ⟦Mark 12:11|Mk 12:11⟧.
